From eb2cda9e164c60d417be34a2f608bf0d89f6e637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rou <shamay1030@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:09:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] runtime: support indexed cached-fresh prefill plan

EXPERIMENTAL, off unless SGLANG_PIC_EXPERIMENTAL_INDEXED_MIXED_PREFILL=1.

A Link could only be laid out as prefix | block ... block | suffix: the
mutable boundary was set once, after the last block, so fresh text between
two cached chunks had no representation. The indexed exact sub-context path
finds cached chunks wherever they sit in a query, so a request can be
fresh | cached | fresh | cached | fresh.

physical_interblock_fresh_token_counts carries one count per gap between
consecutive blocks -- a count of host-owned tokens, like the prefix count.
_prepare_link carves each gap off the Link input, appends it after its
block and makes its positions recompute positions; every later block's
start token, and so its RoPE delta, moves past it. Slots, positions and
remap stay here. Refused without the flag, on a non-normalized layout,
with group promotion, or when the gaps leave no mutable suffix.

reserve_link_sources compared one matched handle per requested position
with the number of distinct keys, so a query using one chunk at two places
failed preflight; it now reserves and releases once per distinct block.
The copy path already handled repeats.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
